      "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{33x+3}{(x-4)(x-1)(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{(x-4)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A+B+C.$",
      "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{33x+3}{(x-4)(x-1)(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{(x-4)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-4)(x-1)(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n33x+3=A(x-1)(x+5)+B(x-4)(x+5)+C(x-4)(x-1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=4$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}33(4)+3 & =A(4-1)(4+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(4-4)(4+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(4-4)(4-1) \\\\ 132+3 & =A(27) \\\\ A & =\\frac{135}{27} \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}33(1)+3 & =A(1-1)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(1-4)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(1-4)(1-1) \\\\ 33+3 & =B(-18) \\\\ B & =\\frac{36}{-18} \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}33(-5)+3 & =A(-5-1)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(-5-4)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(-5-4)(-5-1) \\\\ -165+3 & =C(54) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-162}{54} \\\\ C & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B+C=5+(-2)+(-3)=0.\n$$",
