      "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+10}{(x+4)(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{x+4}+\\frac{B}{x+5}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+4)(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n3x+10=A(x+5)+B(x+4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-4$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-4)+10 & =A(-4+5)+B(-4+4) \\\\ -2 & =A \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-5)+10 & =A(-5+5)+B(-5+4) \\\\ -5 & =-B \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+10}{(x+4)(x+5)}=\\frac{-2}{x+4}+\\frac{5}{x+5}.\n$$",
